<h1>Grab bag</h1>
<h2>September 17, 2026</h2>
I discuss various topics in today’s blog.
<a name="2026-09-17-fuel-price-riots"> </a>
<h3>Fuel price riots</h3>
<p>It would seem that the war against Iran is causing fuel prices to
 skyrocket worldwide, <a href="AI/2026-09-15-FuelRiots.html">resulting in riots across the globe</a>.
<p>Here in Mexico, fuel prices have stayed constant; it helps a lot that
 Mexico has its own source of oil and doesn’t have to rely on foreign
 oil. Prices at gas stations are highly regulated here; the price of gas
 is essentially the same at the local CostCo as it is at a gas station
 in the middle of the desert in northern Mexico.
<a name="2026-09-17-tates-prison-conditions"> </a>
<h3>Tate’s prison conditions</h3>
<p>The Tates are apparently in <a href="AI/2026-09-15-TatesPrison.html">horrible prison  conditions</a>.
<p>Yes, these conditions are inhumane. Maybe having the Tates be under
 these conditions will get the attention of people in charge of the
 prisons, who seem to ignore the problem when brown-skinned people have
 to endure those conditions.
<a name="2026-09-17-dirty-laundry"> </a>
<h3>Dirty laundry</h3>
<p>Don Henley once wrote a song about how unsavory the press can be
 called “Dirty Laundry”.<sup style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 0; vertical-align: 5px"><a id="back-2026-09-17-1"><a href="#2026-09-17-1">1</a></a></sup> 
Seeing how the press is fanning the fires of the Lindsay Clancy
 situation, I can see how much this song still applies today.
<p>First, the left-wing press <a href="https://archive.ph/20260912162426/https://x.com/SueOC_NBCBoston/status/2098499939898732736">doxxed one of Clancy’s  jurors</a>, 
the one who refused to declare
 Clancy not guilty for reasons of insanity.
<p>So the right-wing press retaliates by doxxing <a href="https://archive.ph/20260916211753/https://x.com/HowieCarrShow/status/2100249598748926365">personal information about Clancy’s  lawyer</a>.
<p>The right is now <a href="https://archive.ph/20260917101444/https://x.com/ThePatriotOasis/status/2100309057714221234">painting that same juror as a  hero</a>.
<p>The sensationalist press also posted a woke screed saying the juror
 deserved to be doxxed. <a href="https://archive.ph/20260916013944/https://x.com/bostonherald/status/2099790986247324129">The right was not  amused</a> 
(<a href="https://archive.ph/9T4vO">Alt link</a>).
<p>Here’s one stupid quote from that article: “The jurors voted 11-1 for
 insanity. This indicates that public opinion breaks down along similar
 lines.” Actually, public opinion is, as I type this, <a href="https://yougov.com/en-us/daily-results/20260908-75734-4">46% feel she is guilty, 21% feel she is not guilty by reason of insanity, and 33% are not  sure</a>.
<p>As Don Henley sang many years ago, the press is motivated by our
 baser instincts, with “crap is king; give us dirty laundry” being the
 key lyric from that classic song.<sup style="font-size: 9pt; line-height: 0; vertical-align: 5px"><a id="back-2026-09-17-2"><a href="#2026-09-17-2">2</a></a></sup>

